  ],
  "description": "Three change stories record A-601's Tuesday revisions of fire ratings: chg-7 (\"1.5 h\" to \"90 min\"), chg-8 (\"60 min\" to \"90 min\") and chg-9 (\"1.5 h\" to \"90 min\", approved on Tuesday). A Wednesday normalization of the project names the fixture fire-rating interpretation. chg-7 is open at its effective time and its revision now changes no property: the normalization's write records its end act at Wednesday, cause normalization, and a Tuesday frame still shows it open and awaiting review. chg-8 still changes a property and stays open, compared under the interpretation. chg-9 had ended at its approval and is untouched; when the approval is withdrawn on Thursday, it does not reopen, because the interpretation in force leaves its revision changing nothing: the withdrawal records a period of no length that ends at once by the normalization, and from Thursday the story reads ended and unreviewed with the normalization as its ending, while a Wednesday frame still shows the approval. Only chg-8 is pending.",
  "note": "7.2.7: \"A change story that is open when the interpretation in force for its subject changes (7.3.8), and whose revision changes no property under the interpretation in force from then, ends at that instant, with the normalization whose interpretation is in force from then as its ending record.\" 7.6.2: \"Where the interpretation in force at that withdrawal's effective time leaves the revision changing no property, the period that begins then also ends then, with the normalization that put that interpretation in force as its ending record. That period has no length, is never open (7.6.3) and is the story's last: the story's ending is the review up to that instant, and the normalization from it (7.6.14).\" 6.7.9: \"Where no other review remains in effect and that interpretation leaves the revision changing no property, the story stays ended, and from then its ending is the normalization that put that interpretation in force (7.6.2).\" So step 20 records chg-9/b2 and chg-9/e2, step 21 reads the normalization ending, step 22 reads that end act, and step 23, a Wednesday frame, still reads the review as the ending.",
